*YOU MUST DOCUMENT THE SETUP OF YOUR SHM AND SYNCHRONIZATION PROTOCOL HERE*.
Protocol for IPC using shared memory with POSIX semaphores. Shared memory structure consists of header (containing shmSize and bufSize) followed by semaphores and data buffer. Three semaphores control synchronization: readySem for shared memory access (init=1), clientDataSem for client-to-server signaling (init=0), and serverDataSem for server-to-client signaling (init=0). For data transfer, sender first sends header containing message type and size, then sends data in chunks if needed. The receiver reads header first, then data. For large messages exceeding buffer size, data is split into multiple transfers, each following same synchronization protocol.

